station: A sky rail station's platforms are side platforms at concourse z 24, outer edge 8 m from the line (beamCentres/2 + 0.75 beam + 4 m platform). Each station reaches the street by ≥ 2 stair-and-escalator banks (one each side of the line) and ≥ 1 lift each side; banks land on public ground (pavement, median, mall, park, quay), never on a plot. A megastructure concourse within 30 m joins the station by a skybridge ≥ 5 m wide. Tram stops stay at street level.
bridges: A deck or bridge over a road keeps headroom.road under its structure (z − structureDepth − 0.18 ≥ 5.5); its supports stand in the zones its megastructure lists, never in a carriageway or the tram reservation. A bridge crossing the sky rail line passes ≥ 3 m clear of any pylon.
